  "question": {
    "text": "In Friedel-Crafts alkylation of aniline, one gets:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "tifAR",
      "text": "alkylated product with ortho and para&nbsp;substitution.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4ZFwZ",
      "text": "secondary amine after acidic treatment.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3OWiv",
      "text": "an amide product.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8KQZX",
      "text": "positively charged nitrogen at benzene ring.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Aniline does not undergo Friedel-crafts reaction&nbsp;due to salt formation with aluminium chloride, the Lewis acid, which is used as a catalyst, whereas&nbsp;aniline is a strong base. So, an acid-base reaction will take place. Thus, aniline reacts with <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> to form a salt.<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/75d7b7ac-4e45-493a-91c6-85fa0ddc3273-9711822.png\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 157px;\" /><br />Due to the positive charge on the nitrogen atom (shows <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> effect and it is meta directing), electrophilic substitution in the benzene ring is deactivated. Hence, the Friedel-Crafts reaction will not take place in aniline.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
